---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import Hero from "../components/Hero.astro";
import SectionHeading from "../components/SectionHeading.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About"
  description="Learn about METMA LATAM and the scientific scope of III METMA LATAM 2027."
>
  <Hero
    title="About METMA LATAM"
    subtitle="A regional forum for spatial, temporal, and spatio-temporal statistical modelling."
    location="Santiago, Chile"
    date="1-3 September 2027"
    venue="Pontificia Universidad Catolica de Chile"
  />

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container content-grid">
      <article class="content-block">
        <SectionHeading eyebrow="About the Conference" title="A scientific meeting for modelling data in space and time" />
        <p>
          METMA LATAM is a scientific meeting focused on the development,
          assessment, computation, and application of statistical methods for
          spatial, temporal, and spatio-temporal data. III METMA LATAM 2027 will
          provide a setting for researchers, students, and practitioners to
          exchange ideas across methodological and applied communities.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="content-block">
        <SectionHeading eyebrow="Scientific Scope" title="Theory, methodology, computation, and applications" />
        <p>
          The conference welcomes work on spatial statistics, geostatistics,
          point processes, areal data, spatial extremes, Bayesian spatial models,
          computational methods, machine learning for geospatial data, and
          interdisciplinary applications in environmental sciences, public
          health, climate, ecology, mining, energy, natural resources, urban
          systems, and public policy.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="content-block">
        <SectionHeading eyebrow="Why Latin America" title="Regional questions with global methodological relevance" />
        <p>
          Latin America offers a distinctive landscape for spatio-temporal
          statistical science: diverse ecosystems, rapidly changing cities,
          climate exposure, natural resource systems, public health challenges,
          and large geospatial data streams. METMA LATAM creates room for
          collaboration across countries, disciplines, and modelling traditions.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="content-block">
        <SectionHeading eyebrow="Previous Meetings" title="Extending the METMA tradition" />
        <p>
          METMA-LATAM extends the METMA tradition to Latin America, supporting a
          sustained regional conversation about modern spatial, temporal, and
          spatio-temporal statistical methods. Additional information about
          previous METMA and METMA-LATAM meetings will be linked here once the
          organizing team confirms the reference materials.
        </p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
